committed GasPriceAutoPoll / DevTools / System logs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE RECONCILIATION (no scope narrowing / no parity shortcuts — covenant #2/#5)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web SecurityAccessPage.tsx is a `PageContainer` (title `t('admin.security.title')` +
subtitle `t('admin.security.subtitle')` + the header `VehicleSelect` / `RangePicker` actions)
that, while `loading`, shows a `<Spinner/>` and HIDES its body (`loading ? spinner : children`);
its `error={null}`, so a load failure never blanks the body — it prepends the inline
`<AlertBanner variant="danger">{error.loadFailed}: {detail}</AlertBanner>`. The body renders
the "may not be secure" red panel (GlassPanel1, gated `!isSecure && latest`), the digital-twin
panel (GlassPanel2, gated `latest`), and eight sub-surfaces: SummaryStatsRow,
SecurityStatusCards, WindowStatusDetail, LiveVehicleState, SentryModeChart, SecurityStatistics,
EventHistoryTable, EventTimeline.

Faithful to the source, the native page HOSTS the eight real, already-shipped feature surfaces
(each its OWN already-DONE P4 unit, shipped at apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/*) PLUS the
shared `VehicleTwin` surface (apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/VehicleTwin*) inside
GlassPanel2 — NOT re-stubbed. Every web region is reproduced by its actual component. The page
adds only the web PageContainer chrome (TSPageTitle + subtitle + the two TSSelect header
controls — the SleepEfficiency peer pattern for VehicleSelect/RangePicker), the load-failure
TSAlertBanner, the red GlassPanel1 alert, and the GlassPanel2 twin frame — all bound through an
@Observable SecurityAccessPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view). The page `phase`
(loading / error / success) reproduces the PageContainer branches exactly: a centered spinner
while loading (body hidden), the body otherwise, with the inline error.loadFailed banner
prepended on a load failure (never blanking the body). No section was dropped; nothing stubbed.

The hosted-surface sources default to the representative `SecurityAccessSample` assembly
(the peer `Sample*DataSource` convention); the live useSecurityEvents/useVehicles query
adapters are injected in a later wiring phase without touching this page. The sample reading is
deliberately UNSECURE (locked, doors closed, one window open) so both GlassPanels render — and
`isSecure` is derived from that reading by the REAL `SecurityCardsLogic` (the same shipped
helper the cards use), so the page's secure-state gate matches the cards exactly.

